  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Read the repository in this order",
      "items": [
        "1. flake.nix chooses inputs and exports darwinConfigurations.corthan.",
        "2. hosts/corthan/darwin.nix sets aarch64-darwin, packages and system services.",
        "3. hosts/corthan/home.nix chooses user packages, imports and forced file links.",
        "4. config/ contains the implementation; skills/ contains the operating instructions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How a change reaches the Mac",
      "items": [
        "1. Edit repository sources; include new referenced files in Git before the build.",
        "2. darwin-rebuild build --flake .#corthan builds an immutable system generation.",
        "3. skills/activate-darwin/scripts/activate.applescript activates that exact store path using native administrator authorization.",
        "4. Verify /run/current-system and the affected settings. Build success alone does not activate changes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What is declarative; what remains mutable",
      "items": [
        "Home Manager force=true makes the repository authoritative for managed config and skill links.",
        "Codex and Orca activation hooks reconcile owned appearance keys while preserving application state; Orca defers when open.",
        "cx and cxh share configuration, skills and themes; their authentication and sessions remain separate.",
        "LazyVim downloads plugins at runtime and keeps its lockfile in Neovim state; flake.lock pins the Nix inputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Where to make common changes",
      "items": [
        "Add system/Homebrew apps in hosts/corthan/darwin.nix; add Nix user tools in hosts/corthan/home.nix.",
        "Edit held-key actions in config/keyboard/layout.json and macOS bindings in macos.json; use the keyboard detail map for ownership.",
        "Edit Neovim Lua under config/nvim/lua/ and terminal integrations under config/ghostty/ and config/herdr*/.",
        "Theme modules live in config/codex/, config/orca/ and config/wallpaper.nix; operating knowledge belongs beside the owning skill."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Scope and boundaries",
      "items": [
        "This is one personal workstation configuration, corthan, for the user nick on Apple Silicon.",
        "Determinate owns Nix and its daemon: nix-darwin sets nix.enable=false.",
        "Homebrew is declared through nix-darwin; Bartender, Node.js and enabled CLI programs use Nix/Home Manager.",
        "The diagram summarizes configuration ownership. Keyboard runtime services are expanded in keyboard.html; configured launch targets do not prove an app is installed."
      ]
    }
  ]
